# {{.Project}}

Your API{{if .Web}}, a web app for your customers{{end}}{{if .Console}}, and a console for your staff{{end}}, behind Plat5. Plat5 signs people in, keeps organizations and their members, roles, and keys, checks every request at its gateway, and records an audit log. Your code does none of that: it reads the organization from the path.

Everything here is yours to change. It is a starting point, not a dependency.

## Run it

```bash
plat5 start     # Plat5, then your apps; prints every link, login, and a key
plat5 status    # the same, again
plat5 logs --app
plat5 stop      # data is kept
```

{{if .Web}}Sign in to the web app as `{{.DevEmail}}` / `{{.Password}}`.{{end}}{{if .Console}} Sign in to the staff console as `{{.StaffEmail}}` / `{{.Password}}`.{{end}} Edit any app and it reloads.

